{
 "slug": "test/export-menus",
 "about": "The two other menus that export or share, in every edition: Saved Measurements' library menu ('panel') and Analysis Results' ('analysisResults'). Each has one button — its word on each platform in 'button' ('mac' and 'ios' are Swift's, 'python' and 'web' the others'), its SF Symbol and Material Design icon — and items in groups between separators, as saved-measurement-menu.json: an item with no title for a platform is not on that platform's menu, and a group left empty is not shown. Each item has its icon, as the Delete menu's do: Share's, Export's (a measurement menu's Export Measurement), and Selected's tick (as Delete's Selected…); Analysis Results' items have a measurement menu's icons for the same items. Export writes the file through a save dialog; Share opens the share sheet, which only Swift has; Selected ticks the measurements first, as Delete's Selected… does. '…' as style guide S9.",
